+# Changelog
+
+All notable changes to tally are documented here.
+Format follows [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/).
+
+## [Unreleased] — targeting 2.1
+
+### Added
+
+- **`budget` subcommand** — `tally budget --month YYYY-MM` prints each
+  budgeted category alongside its month-to-date spending and a three-state
+  indicator: `ok`, `warn` (≥ 80 % of the limit), or `over` (exceeds the
+  limit).
+- **`CATEGORY_BUDGETS`** in `tally/config.py` — monthly USD limits per
+  category (`food` $600, `transport` $200, `rent` $1 500, `entertainment`
+  $150, `other` $300).
+- **`BUDGET_WARN_RATIO`** in `tally/config.py` — configurable threshold
+  (default `0.8`) at which the budget report switches from `ok` to `warn`.
+- **`budget_status()`** in `tally/report.py` — core logic that compares a
+  month's per-category totals against `CATEGORY_BUDGETS` and returns the
+  structured list consumed by `cmd_budget`.
